# Citation metadata for LaNet-vi (https://citation-file-format.github.io/).
# GitHub renders this as the "Cite this repository" entry. Keep `version` and
# `date-released` in step with the release (see CONTRIBUTING.md, "Releasing").
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use LaNet-vi in your research, please cite the software and the papers below."
type: software
title: "LaNet-vi: large scale network visualization by k-core, k-dense and d-core decomposition"
abstract: >-
  LaNet-vi visualizes large networks by k-core, k-dense (m-core) and d-core decomposition,
  laying nodes out in concentric rings by shell index and rendering the result with matplotlib.
  Version 5 is a Python rewrite of the original C++ tool developed at Universidad de Buenos
  Aires / CONICET.
